# IoT-Based Industrial Machine Monitoring and Cable Fault Visualization Using ESP8266

This project demonstrates an IoT-based industrial monitoring system using the ESP8266 NodeMCU. It continuously monitors machine temperature, vibration, and cable fault conditions while displaying live data on a web dashboard over a WiFi network.

## Project Overview

The objective of this project is to improve industrial machine monitoring by providing real-time sensor data and cable fault visualization through an embedded web server.

## Features

- Real-time temperature monitoring using DHT11
- Machine vibration detection using SW-420 sensor
- Cable fault visualization using potentiometer simulation
- Live web dashboard using ESP8266 Web Server
- Alarm indication using buzzer
- Push-button alarm acknowledgement
- WiFi-based monitoring

## Hardware Used

- ESP8266 NodeMCU
- DHT11 Temperature & Humidity Sensor
- SW-420 Vibration Sensor
- Potentiometer
- Push Button
- Buzzer
- Breadboard
- Jumper Wires

## Software & Tools

- Arduino IDE
- Embedded C
- ESP8266 Web Server
- HTML
- CSS
- GitHub

